{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Session handoff — the change MERGED but the ticket is not closeable as-is\n\nState at handoff: `in_progress`. **Gerrit 1975 merged as `c504977aef`** (verified: one commit on\n`origin/main` carries this ticket's trailer). **No attestation of any kind** is recorded — neither\nplan-review nor completion.\n\n**Blocker: 0 of 5 ACs are ticked.** I am not ticking them; this session did not verify them.\n\n**One AC deserves particular care** — *\"Every existing `gate_enabled` caller is updated to handle\nthe third state explicitly\"* — because it is a caller-sweep claim, and this session repeatedly\nfound caller sweeps to be the thing that was incomplete. Verify it with **both** instruments, not\none: Serena's `find_referencing_symbols` for the semantic reference set, **and** a plain `grep`\nfor the symbol name as a string, since the LSP cannot resolve `getattr`/`monkeypatch.setattr`\ntargets and returns an empty result rather than an error. An empty semantic result is not\nevidence of absence.\n\n**Relevant context from this session:** `steep-tired-whimbrel`'s subject — `gate_enabled` failing\nOPEN and collapsing gate-off with config-unreadable — is the same fail-open family catalogued in\n`sphinxian-agrarian-snake` (twelve instances). It is also cited as a live blocker in another open\nticket's design notes, where the enum being proposed \"cannot be produced without changing that\nfunction's signature.\" Whoever closes this should check whether the merged change actually\nresolved that dependency or merely moved it.\n\n**What the next session should do:** verify the five ACs against merged `c504977aef`, tick only\nwhat is observed, and close through the completion verifier. If the close gate demands a\nplan-review attestation that was never created, that is itself worth recording rather than\nforcing with `--force`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787329335612060001,"uuid":"09b893d8-7add-4fe4-9c15-9f5448999e38"}